# 2. 3D Draft

## Aim
With reference to the drawings in the task folder, to 3D draft three machine parts in Fusion 360.

All three parts were modelled in the Design workspace (Solid tab), with document units set to **mm, g**. Each part follows the same workflow: draw a fully dimensioned 2D sketch from the reference drawing, then turn it into a solid with extrude or revolve.

| Part | Description | Main tools |
|------|-------------|------------|
| 1 | Hexagonal base with a cylindrical top | Sketch, Extrude |
| 2 | Disc with notched bolt holes and a hex bore | Sketch, Extrude, Cut, Hole |
| 3 | Stepped shaft with a double-cone section | Sketch, Revolve |

---

## Part 1: Hexagonal base with cylindrical top

### Sketch
- A regular hexagon with an edge length of **29.30 mm**.
- Two concentric circles inside it: **Ø45.00 mm** and **Ø35.50 mm**.

![Part 1 sketch](images/part1_sketch.png)

### Steps
1. Draw the hexagon with the Polygon tool and dimension its edge as 29.30 mm.
2. Draw the two concentric circles at the centre of the hexagon and dimension them Ø45.00 and Ø35.50 mm.
3. Extrude the hexagon to form the base.
4. Extrude the Ø45 circle on top of the base to form the cylinder.
5. The Ø35.50 circle defines the inner opening of the cylinder, so it is left as the inner ring on the top face.

### 3D model
A hexagonal base carrying a round cylinder with an inner ring on the top face.

![Part 1 3D model](images/part1_model.png)

